# Static-analysis and formatting harness. This spec describes the contract; the machine-
# readable settings live in /Cargo.toml and ./rustfmt.toml. Crate and file specs inherit this
# harness through the root vynil spec and never restate its rule levels.

Spec: linting

Platform: Rust/clippy/rustfmt

Purpose:
  Define the static-analysis and formatting harness that every crate obeys so agents and humans
  get the same strict, deterministic guidance, with the harshest rules aimed squarely at new
  code. The harness is a contract for implementation, not documentation of taste.

Structure:
  /Cargo.toml: Defines the [workspace.lints.clippy] and [workspace.lints.rust] levels shared
    by every crate
  ./rustfmt.toml: Shared nightly rustfmt settings
  ./specdd/bootstrap.project.md: Records the operational rule tying code to clippy-clean
    verification (not a spec target)

Owns:
  ./rustfmt.toml

Can modify:
  /Cargo.toml: the [workspace.lints] block only

Must:
  Deny `clippy::pedantic` at workspace level and warn `clippy::nursery`, with pedantic prioritised
    so nursery does not override it.
  Deny `clippy::dbg_macro`, `clippy::todo`, and `clippy::unimplemented` at workspace level.
  Warn `unsafe_code` and `missing_debug_implementations` at workspace level.
  Carry, at each crate root, a `#![cfg_attr(not(test), deny(clippy::unwrap_used,
    clippy::expect_used))]` attribute so tests keep unwrap and expect and product code may not.
  Carry at each crate root a warn for `clippy::arithmetic_side_effects` and
    `clippy::indexing_slicing`, and promote either to deny per-file once the sites are addressed.
  Require clippy and fmt as part of every verification loop, so code that changes is code that
    passes both.

Must not:
  Silence a harness rule with an `#[allow(...)]` in product code unless the owning file spec
    records the concrete reason.
  Set `unwrap_used` or `expect_used` in the `[workspace.lints]` table; the per-crate cfg_attr form
    is what keeps them test-exempt.

Depends on:
  /Cargo.toml
  nightly rustfmt

Done when:
  Every crate opts into the workspace lints, every crate root carries the deny and warn
    attributes, and every `Scenario` below has a test or is covered by tooling.

Scenario: product unwrap is refused
  Given a product-code call site uses `unwrap()`
  And the crate root carries the deny attributes
  When `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` runs
  Then the lint fails the build

Scenario: test unwrap is allowed
  Given a `#[cfg(test)]` test uses `unwrap()`
  When `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` runs
  Then the test code emits no unwrap warning

Scenario: pedantic is a hard error
  Given new code introduces a pedantic-level clippy warning
  When clippy runs with the workspace lints table
  Then the check fails at deny
